## Lotte Chilsung Beverage Co., Ltd. financial statements, 6 years: Back to a profit in 2021 after a net loss of KRW 16.8bn in 2020

The consolidated financial statements in the 2020–2025 annual reports that Lotte Chilsung Beverage Co., Ltd. (005300) filed with Korea's DART electronic disclosure system, laid out by year. Figures from the 2026 third-quarter report cover a different period and are shown separately. **Every figure below is taken as filed in the DART submissions; there is no interpretation or outlook.** Amounts are in Korean won (KRW; bn = billion, tn = trillion).

### 1. Income statement — the sign of net income changed in 2021

| Fiscal year | Revenue | Revenue change | Operating income | Op. income change | Operating margin | Net income |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | 2.26tn | — | 97.2bn | — | 4.3% | −16.8bn |
| 2021 | 2.51tn | +10.99% | 182.2bn | +87.41% | 7.3% | 137.1bn |
| 2022 | 2.84tn | +13.39% | 222.9bn | +22.30% | 7.8% | 131.1bn |
| 2023 | 3.22tn | +13.48% | 210.7bn | −5.47% | 6.5% | 166.5bn |
| 2024 | 4.02tn | +24.80% | 184.9bn | −12.22% | 4.6% | 60.0bn |
| 2025 | 3.97tn | −1.33% | 167.2bn | −9.61% | 4.2% | 51.2bn |

Revenue was largest in 2024 at KRW 4.02tn and smallest in 2020 at KRW 2.26tn among the six years. It fell from the previous year once: 2025 (−1.33%).

Operating income was largest in 2022 at KRW 222.9bn and smallest in 2020 at KRW 97.2bn. The operating margin was highest in 2022 at 7.8%.

**Net income was largest in 2023 at KRW 166.5bn and smallest in 2020 at KRW −16.8bn.**

### 2. Financial position — equity became 1.23x

| Fiscal year | Total assets | Total equity | Debt ratio | Current ratio |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | 3.47tn | 1.30tn | 165.6% | 103.3% |
| 2021 | 3.60tn | 1.45tn | 148.9% | 102.4% |
| 2022 | 3.70tn | 1.41tn | 161.7% | 88.3% |
| 2023 | 4.26tn | 1.54tn | 177.0% | 90.9% |
| 2024 | 4.37tn | 1.58tn | 177.0% | 76.7% |
| 2025 | 4.28tn | 1.60tn | 167.7% | 77.8% |

The debt ratio was highest in 2023 at 177.0% and lowest in 2021 at 148.9%.

Over the same period total assets went from KRW 3.47tn to KRW 4.28tn (1.24x), and **total equity went from KRW 1.30tn to KRW 1.60tn and became 1.23x.**

The current ratio was below 100% in 4 years, 2022, 2023, 2024 and 2025 — in those years current liabilities exceeded current assets.

